{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDfpu3USuaU9GnLe7gs4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed R14 and A01–A04 and saved the results to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The `--batch R14,A01,A02,A03,A04 --before-challenges` validation prints `Valid`. The result is four gaps and one needs_evidence. I didn't run challenges, and I left the other items alone.\n\nI made two judgement calls:\n- **R14 rating:** I rated R14 needs_evidence instead of na_candidate. The validator wants an evidence entry for an N/A rating, and I found no recovery code to cite. This is a deliberate downgrade from N/A.\n- **Scope text:** I replaced the scope TODO in the findings file by editing the JSON directly, not through `answer.py`.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| A01 | gap | The token cache is keyed by audience, scope and tenant only (`app/identity.py:95`), so a token minted for one user is reused for other users in that tenant. The user also goes to the token service as a plain string (`identity.py:109`). A01.4 is unknown because no RBAC or token-service grants are in the repo. |\n| A02 | gap | The audit schema and writer require all six fields. But refusals before `run_started` write no audit record: kill-switch and quota checks (`app/loop.py:127`, `loop.py:129`), auth failures (`app/main.py:135`, `main.py:138`), and Slack approval decisions (`main.py:181`). |\n| A03 | gap | The prompts go into the agent-type-id hash by path only, not content hash (`identity.py:68`, `identity.py:69`), so editing a prompt doesn't change the ID. The model pinning, sorted serialization and no-secrets checks passed. |\n| A04 | gap | `memory_read` takes the tenant from the model-supplied `business_unit` argument (`app/tools/memory.py:44`), which allows cross-tenant reads. A04.4 is unknown because the Slack approval handoff has no trace context. A04.3 passed. |\n| R14 | needs_evidence | I found no checkpoint, recovery or replay code, so N/A looks likely but isn't established. `pay_invoice` sends a deterministic `Idempotency-Key` (`app/tools/payments.py:33`). |\n\nThe 7 prescan hits all map to other items (B07, B08, B09, B11, R05), so I left them for the batches that own those items.\n\nI ran inventory and the prescan through `skill/scripts`. `-I` broke the skill's sibling imports, so those scripts ran without it. Besides the findings file, I created `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` in `agent/`, and `ledgers/` in the workspace root (coverage ledger inputs and helper scripts)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":102919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":769,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5292746-1a96-40a3-b992-fda76a19632e","uuid":"29edd9e5-3e53-48fc-8363-5826b59e8ab7","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:46:16.670Z","request_id":"req_011CgDfptiPJCqTCX7y2Uan6"}
